WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.560
Across the world today, many
Christians are led by bishops,

2
00:00:03.610 --> 00:00:05.600
priests and deacons.

3
00:00:05.650 --> 00:00:08.030
Other churches have no bishops at all.

4
00:00:08.080 --> 00:00:10.990
Ministers and elders govern them instead.

5
00:00:11.040 --> 00:00:13.720
Both sides read the same New Testament.

6
00:00:13.770 --> 00:00:17.140
The Greek word for bishop
simply means overseer.

7
00:00:17.190 --> 00:00:19.590
So where did bishops come from?

8
00:00:19.640 --> 00:00:21.970
In this mission, you'll
trace the evidence,

9
00:00:22.020 --> 00:00:26.490
from Paul's letters to a bishop writing
on his way to martyrdom in Rome.

10
00:00:26.540 --> 00:00:31.400
Then you'll weigh how much authority the
Bishop of Rome had in the early church.

11
00:00:31.450 --> 00:00:34.530
Your mission: find out
where bishops came from,

12
00:00:34.580 --> 00:00:37.070
and why it still divides churches today.
